claim.claim-text:
obtaining M of reference images for machine learning;
pre-increasing the reference images for N patterns to obtain M×N of images;
picking up a predetermined image from the M×N of the images, and performing random geometric transformation involving 90×L degree rotation and inversion or non-inversion;
inputting the reference image having undergone geometric transformation into a neural network for machine learning; and
repeating the geometric transformation and machine learning until a number of repeated times reaches a necessary time to create an ensemble identifier (14a), wherein M and N are each an integer equal to or greater than 2, and L is an integer of 0 to 3.

inputting a query image to be predicted;
pre-increasing the query image for N patterns to obtain N of the query images;
causing each of the N of the query images to be subjected to geometric transformation for 8 patterns involving a combination of 90×L degree rotation and inversion or non-inversion;
individually inputting 8×N of the picked-up images having undergone the geometric transformation to an ensemble identifier (14a) that has performed machine learning by inputting at least one reference image including a reference image having undergone geometric transformation into a neural network, to obtain 8×N of inference values; and
averaging the 8×N of the inference values to obtain an eventual inference value, wherein
N is an integer that is equal to or greater than 2 and L is an integer of 0 to 3.

M of the picked-up images are obtained as reference images for machine learning;
the picked-up images are pre-increased for N patterns to obtain M×N of the images;
a predetermined image is picked up from the M×N of the images, random geometric transformation involving 90×L degree rotation and inversion or non-inversion is performed;
the picked-up image having undergone the geometric transformation is input into a neural network for machine learning; and
the geometric transformation and machine learning are repeated until a number of repeated times reaches a necessary time to create an ensemble identifier (14a), wherein
M and N are each an integer equal to or greater than 2, and L is an integer of 0 to 3.

a picked-up image to be predicted is input as a query image;
the picked-up image is pre-increased for N patterns to obtain N of the picked-up images;
each of the N of the picked-up image is subjected to geometric transformation for 8 patterns involving a combination of 90×L degree rotation and inversion or non-inversion;
8×N of the picked-up images having undergone the geometric transformation are individually input to an ensemble identifier (14a) that has performed machine learning by inputting at least one reference image including a reference image having undergone geometric transformation into a neural network, to obtain 8×N of inference values; and
average the 8×N of the inference values are averaged to obtain an eventual inference value, wherein
N is an integer that is equal to or greater than 2 and L is an integer of 0 to 3.
